{"title":"2022 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The arrows on the two spinners shown below are spun. Let the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />  equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times the number on Spinner <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c43070a2acf8f4e25d98e48c404d9348a26d40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, added to the number on Spinner <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09920c3af0daa12ac2ec5174e737c31e0f8cec75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{B}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />. What is the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is a perfect square number?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/636fbab7e24e0ba932ae7a1c7fe84a461d7d0239.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] //diagram by pog size(6cm); usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;); filldraw(arc((0,0), r=4, angle1=0, angle2=90)--(0,0)--cycle,mediumgray*0.5+gray*0.5); filldraw(arc((0,0), r=4, angle1=90, angle2=180)--(0,0)--cycle,lightgray); filldraw(arc((0,0), r=4, angle1=180, angle2=270)--(0,0)--cycle,mediumgray); filldraw(arc((0,0), r=4, angle1=270, angle2=360)--(0,0)--cycle,lightgray*0.5+mediumgray*0.5); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, (-1.5,1.7)); label(&quot;$6$&quot;, (1.5,1.7)); label(&quot;$7$&quot;, (1.5,-1.7)); label(&quot;$8$&quot;, (-1.5,-1.7)); label(&quot;Spinner A&quot;, (0, -5.5)); filldraw(arc((12,0), r=4, angle1=0, angle2=90)--(12,0)--cycle,mediumgray*0.5+gray*0.5); filldraw(arc((12,0), r=4, angle1=90, angle2=180)--(12,0)--cycle,lightgray); filldraw(arc((12,0), r=4, angle1=180, angle2=270)--(12,0)--cycle,mediumgray); filldraw(arc((12,0), r=4, angle1=270, angle2=360)--(12,0)--cycle,lightgray*0.5+mediumgray*0.5); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (10.5,1.7)); label(&quot;$2$&quot;, (13.5,1.7)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (13.5,-1.7)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;, (10.5,-1.7)); label(&quot;Spinner B&quot;, (12, -5.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"148\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/559a646c5d8a99360021772cf2027f8c8c8168f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~\\dfrac{1}{16}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~\\dfrac{1}{8}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~\\dfrac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~\\dfrac{3}{8}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we calculate that there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/92251f81dfcd78c67dd057d81543703f31419fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot4=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> possibilities. Now, we list all of two-digit perfect squares. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> are the only ones that can be made using the spinner. Consequently, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f47aebe062e5036c03fc811b87f0ae9b65c7b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{16}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\dfrac{1}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"107\" height=\"49\" /> probability that the number formed by the two spinners is a perfect square.\n</p><p>~MathFun1000\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c0637a8a49dd1bc93c7ea16d0b1d22c26f9714e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> total possibilities of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba8b53452d1df87a9a9f1c2b6c61f360a3a433d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=10A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" />, which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a number from spinner <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is a number from spinner <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Also, notice that there are no perfect squares in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />s or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />s, so only  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f0119d2c68cde8369232a53eaff7ffc5c582b7ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-2=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> values of N work, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f47aebe062e5036c03fc811b87f0ae9b65c7b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{16}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\dfrac{1}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"107\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<pre>We can see that the smallest number on the spinner 1 is 5. Possibilities for 5 are 51,52,53, and 54\n</pre>\n<p>Second one is 6 in which we get 61,62,63,64. We see that 64 is a square number.\nThe next number is 7. Possibilities are 71,72,73, and 74. None of them are squares.\nFinally, we have 8. 81,82,83, and 84 are the numbers possible. 81 is a perfect square.\nAs our trusty probability formula tells us, probability is the number of desired outcomes over possible outcomes.\nThe possible outcomes are 16 and the desired outcomes are 2. The fraction is 2/16. In simplest terms, it is 1/8.\nBringing to answer choice (B)\n~ I would like to stay anonymous\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tYWp6fcUAik?si=V8hv_zOn_zYOi9E5&amp;t=1458\">https://youtu.be/tYWp6fcUAik?si=V8hv_zOn_zYOi9E5&amp;t=1458</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/oUEa7AjMF2A?si=NvktZSXqcd8LE9yU&amp;t=1604\">https://youtu.be/oUEa7AjMF2A?si=NvktZSXqcd8LE9yU&amp;t=1604</a> \n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Flq6oB23_WM\">https://youtu.be/Flq6oB23_WM</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ij9pAy6tQSg?t=1008\">https://youtu.be/Ij9pAy6tQSg?t=1008</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/p29Fe2dLGs8?t=58\">https://youtu.be/p29Fe2dLGs8?t=58</a>\n</p><p>~STEMbreezy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Wrbpq4D5F18\">https://youtu.be/Wrbpq4D5F18</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/U6eqFrD7BXA\">https://youtu.be/U6eqFrD7BXA</a>\n</p><p>~harungurcan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span><span class=\